@startuml
title SysMon - Container Deployment Sequence Diagram

participant "SysMon Frontend" as Frontend
participant "SysMon Backend" as Backend
participant "SysMon Authentication System" as Auth
participant "Container Engine" as Engine

note over Frontend
  Admin (Tier 2 or 3) opens Create Container
  and selects Visual Builder.
end note

== Load the groups assigned to the admin ==
Frontend -> Backend : GET /v1/compute-groups\nAuthorization: Bearer token
Backend --> Frontend : 200 OK\n{items, page, pageSize, total}
Frontend -> Backend : GET /v1/storage-groups\nAuthorization: Bearer token
Backend --> Frontend : 200 OK\n{items, page, pageSize, total}

note over Frontend
  Admin enters the image repository tag, selects the
  Compute Group, maps data to a Storage Group folder,
  selects Docker or Podman and clicks Deploy.
end note

== Deploy ==
Frontend -> Backend : POST /v1/containers\nAuthorization: Bearer token\nIdempotency-Key: key\n{image, engine, computeGroupId,\nstorageGroupId, volumes}
Backend -> Auth : GET /v1/auth/validate\nAuthorization: Bearer token
Auth --> Backend : 200 OK {userId, tier}\nor 401 Unauthorized

alt Token missing, invalid or expired
  Backend --> Frontend : 401 Unauthorized\n{code, message}
else Caller may not create containers or use the chosen groups
  Backend --> Frontend : 403 Forbidden\n{code, message}
else Compute Group or Storage Group does not exist
  Backend --> Frontend : 404 Not Found\n{code, message}
else Data invalid (empty image tag, path outside Storage Group)
  Backend --> Frontend : 422 Unprocessable Entity\n{code, field, message}
else Storage Group quota exceeded
  Backend --> Frontend : 409 Conflict\n{code, message}
else All checks passed
  Backend -> Backend : Inject Compute Group resource limits
  Backend -> Backend : Insert approved Storage Group host paths
  Backend -> Backend : Generate docker-compose.yml
  Backend -> Engine : POST /containers/create\n(from the generated Compose file)

  alt Engine daemon reachable
    Engine --> Backend : 201 Created {Id}
    Backend -> Engine : POST /containers/{Id}/start
    Engine --> Backend : 204 No Content
    Backend --> Frontend : 201 Created\nLocation: /v1/containers/{containerId}\n{containerId, status, image, engine, ...}

    Frontend -> Backend : GET /v1/containers/{containerId}/telemetry\nAccept: text/event-stream
    Backend --> Frontend : 200 OK (event stream)
    loop While the container runs
      Backend --> Frontend : event {timestamp, cpuPercent,\nmemoryBytes, diskBytes}
    end
  else Engine daemon does not answer in time
    note right of Engine : No answer from the engine daemon
    Backend -> Backend : Save generated Compose file as draft
    Backend --> Frontend : 503 Service Unavailable\n{code, message, details: draftId}
  end
end

@enduml
